      "problem": "Evaluate $(-\\frac{1}{3})÷((-4)^{3}÷8).$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)^{3}÷8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-4)^{3}÷8 & = \\\\ (-64)÷8 & = \\\\ \\frac{(-64)}{8} & = \\\\ -8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-\\frac{1}{3})÷((-4)^{3}÷8) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})÷(-8) & = \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{3})\\times (-\\frac{1}{8}) & = \\\\ \\frac{1\\times 1}{3\\times 8} & = \\\\ \\frac{1}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
